## 4. File Change Summary

| File Path | Action | Component / Section | Change Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `src/views/QuickChatView.vue` | Modify | `template` (root `div`) | Added an accessible, opaque loading-splash overlay (`fixed inset-0 z-[60]`, DaisyUI `loading-spinner loading-lg text-primary` + "Loading chat…" label) shown while `chatLoading` is `true`, wrapped in the existing `fade` transition. |
| `src/views/QuickChatView.vue` | Modify | `data()` | Removed the now-unused `loadingTimeout` field (was only used by the deleted timer). |
| `src/views/QuickChatView.vue` | Modify | `unmounted()` | Removed `clearTimeout(this.loadingTimeout)`. |
| `src/views/QuickChatView.vue` | Modify | `watch` | Removed the `activeChatId` watcher that drove the fragile 600 ms splash timer. |
| `src/views/QuickChatView.vue` | Modify | `methods.openChat()` | Now sets `chatLoading = true` only when the URL chat is not cached, and clears it in `finally` — guaranteeing the splash stays for the whole (possibly slow) load and never flashes for already-loaded chats. |
| `src/views/QuickChatView.vue` | Modify | `methods.onActiveChatIdChange()` | Removed (dead code that mismanaged `chatLoading` on unrelated in-app chat switches). |

**Accessibility notes:** the splash uses `role="status"`, `aria-live="polite"` and `aria-busy="true"` so screen readers announce the loading state; opacity `fade` respects the existing 250 ms transition and the overlay is fully opaque (`bg-base-300`) to mask the underlying empty-state greeting flash.

