## 5. Anti-Patterns Avoided
- ❌ **Timing-dependent flags**: the old data `chatLoading` missed the `created()` → `loadProfiles()` await window, letting the input box flash. A computed derived purely from route + resolved data has no such gap.
- ❌ **Hiding only the input while the greeting flashes**: the entire empty-state block is gated, so there is no "What's next…" flash behind the splash.
- ❌ **Two sources of truth**: `activeChat` (computed) still drives the ChatView; `chatLoading` is a pure function of it, so they can never disagree.

## 6. Accessibility Checklist
- ✅ Splash keeps `role="status"`, `aria-live="polite"`, `aria-busy="true"` → screen readers announce "Loading chat…".
- ✅ Input box is **removed from the DOM** (not just visually hidden) during load, so it is not focusable/tabbable.
- ✅ Fully opaque overlay (`bg-base-300`) prevents accidental interaction with underlying content.
- ✅ Existing `fade` (250 ms) transition retained; no motion added.

